/**
\page mp3x_internals mp3x frame analyzer - internals

The GTK4 frame analyzer is built from four implementation units:
mp3x_core.c holds the toolkit-independent engine, mp3x_plot.c the Cairo drawing
layer, mp3x_session.c the per-file lifecycle, and mp3x_ui.c the application,
window and menus. Comments in them cite gtkanal.c and gpkplotting.c where a
constant, a default or a transform reproduces the behaviour of the GTK 1.2
predecessor those files implemented; the files themselves are no longer in the
tree and are reachable through the version history.

What the analyzer looks like to someone using it - the graphs, the display
controls and the keyboard - is described in the mp3x(1) manual page, not here.

\section mp3x_internals_lifetime Architecture and lifetime

\c Mp3xDriver is process and UI lifetime state. It borrows the application and
window, and owns the current session, menu model, CSS provider, view
preferences, async-request identity slots, session-generation counter, and the
cumulative analysis-failure exit latch.

\c Mp3xSession is one open input. It owns its \c lame_t, path and display name,
and transport state. Closing removes its idle source first, shuts down the core
decoder, calls \c close_infile(), closes the LAME handle and frees its strings.
Opening another file restores the captured startup frontend-global baseline, so
options given on the command line cannot leak into a later GUI-selected file.

Each file-dialog request owns a strong driver reference, a dialog, a
cancellable, and one matching \c g_application_hold(); its completion route
releases all four. Each idle source owns a strong driver reference plus the
captured session pointer and generation, and frees them in its destroy notify.

\note A stale async callback must match **both** the driver state epoch and the
session generation before touching session state. That pairing is what makes it
safe for a dialog to complete after the file it was opened for has been closed.

The GUI prevalidates a selected \c GFile before retiring the current session, so
an unusable selection never costs the user the file they already had open. A
successful \c Mp3xPrevalidateResult owns its three strings until they are either
cleared or stolen by the replacement session.

\section mp3x_internals_transport Transport and end of input

Input exhaustion and display completion are different states, and conflating
them is the easiest way to lose the last frames of a file.

For PCM input, the first mp3x_core_step() that returns zero has already shifted
the ring, called \c lame_encode_flush() once, fed its complete output to HIP,
and decoded at most one queued frame. The session then performs exactly
<tt>READ_AHEAD - 1</tt> mp3x_core_drain_step() shifts. Their first calls collect
any remaining HIP output already queued by the flush; once HIP needs more data
they shift invalid sentinels. Drain steps do no input, encoding or statistics
work.

Completion is set only when the final real frame reaches the display position.
Play, repeated Step, and Last/Advance therefore all reach the same final frame,
with its correctly mapped re-synthesis companion.

\c frames_done counts real analyzed frames only, and every real plotting slot
stores <tt>totbits == sum(mainbits[gr][ch])</tt>. A negative core result stops
the session and latches process exit status 1; a later successful open does not
erase it.

\section mp3x_internals_cli Command line

Initial command-line parsing happens before the \c GtkApplication is created.
The existing parser's informational result prints help, version, license, usage,
long help or the genre list once and exits 0 without a window. Parser and open
failures exit non-zero. A successfully opened command-line session is installed
when GTK activates. Subsequent GUI opens use documented clean defaults rather
than replaying the initial argv.

\section mp3x_internals_plot Plotting and export

On-screen titles use a Pango layout created from the drawing widget, inheriting
its font map, font description, direction, DPI and desktop text scaling.
Offscreen PNGs use a deterministic PangoCairo \c "Sans 11" layout instead, so a
saved image does not vary with the desktop it was produced on. A measured title
band is excluded from every graph's data mapping, and drawing areas publish
accessible labels.

Every PNG writer checks the image surface, the Cairo context and the
\c cairo_surface_write_to_png() status. Interactive Save and Export report the
returned error rather than claiming success.

\section mp3x_internals_hooks Test-only instrumentation

Production builds contain no environment-variable automation behaviour at all.
The hooks below are compiled only when \c MP3X_ENABLE_TEST_HOOKS is defined:

\code
./configure --enable-mp3x CPPFLAGS=-DMP3X_ENABLE_TEST_HOOKS
make
\endcode

\warning There is no configure option for this, deliberately - the define is the
only door, and it is meant to be awkward. Confirming that a normal binary
contains none of the \c MP3X_ strings is part of the regression routine below.

Only that build recognises:

- \c MP3X_START_PAUSED - analyze one transition, then wait.
- \c MP3X_STEP_TO_END - exercise repeated paused Step transitions to completion.
- \c MP3X_ADVANCE_TO_END - exercise Last/Advance-to-end.
- \c MP3X_QUIT_WHEN_DONE - quit after completion or injected failure.
- \c MP3X_FAIL_AFTER=N - inject an analyzer failure after N real frames.
- \c MP3X_STATE_REPORT=path - write the final frame, drain and \c totbits
  invariants, plus the final re-synthesis companion offset and decoded PCM peak.
- \c MP3X_SHOT, \c MP3X_SHOT_RESYNTH, \c MP3X_SHOT_MDCT, \c MP3X_SHOT_MDCT1,
  \c MP3X_SHOT_PSY, \c MP3X_SHOT_PSY1, \c MP3X_SHOT_SFB, \c MP3X_SHOT_SFB1,
  \c MP3X_SHOT_COMPOSITE - save all nine final plot artifacts.
- \c MP3X_CHANNEL, \c MP3X_MS, \c MP3X_DIFF, \c MP3X_SOURCE, \c MP3X_NOSFBLINES,
  \c MP3X_KBFLAG - override display choices.

\section mp3x_internals_regression Suggested regression matrix

-# Fresh normal and instrumented builds; changed files warning-clean.
-# Timeout-bound every informational command-line route and one invalid option.
-# WAV, AIFF and MP3 inputs both shorter and longer than \c READ_AHEAD.
-# Play, repeated Step, and Last/Advance to the same final displayed frame.
-# Verify every reported \c totbits against the four \c mainbits fields, and
   require a re-synthesis companion for every displayed final frame. A silent
   fixture may legitimately report a zero decoded PCM peak.
-# Empty, directory, missing, unreadable and non-regular selections.
-# Repeated open, recent, close, cancel and save cycles under the platform leak
   tool.
-# All nine PNG save routes, including an unwritable destination.
-# Channel, source, difference, SFB, subblock and spectrum controls; statistics;
   keyboard transport; fullscreen; and file replacement.
-# Confirm a normal binary contains none of the \c MP3X_ hook strings.

*/
